Engine: editor debugging on non-Windows platforms through files

The engine only created an editor debugger on Windows (named pipes); elsewhere
--enabledebugger quit with "editor_debugger is NULL", and breaking into the
debugger and reporting script errors were compiled out. FileBasedAGSDebugger
already existed but was unused.

"--enabledebugger <token> [<comm-type>[=<config>]]" selects how the engine
talks to the editor: "pipe" (named pipes, Windows only, as before) or "file"
(FileBasedAGSDebugger, every platform). Without a comm-type the platform
default is used: pipes on Windows, files elsewhere. The config is a
comma-separated key:value list handled by the communication class; the file
debugger knows "dir" (folder for its files). Its files are named after the
token (dbgsend_<token>.tmp / dbgrecv_<token>.tmp) and messages are written
atomically (temporary file + rename). break_into_debugger() and
send_exception_to_debugger() work on all platforms; only SetForegroundWindow
stays Windows-specific.

Used by ags4mac (macOS editor port) for breakpoints and stepping.
Branch engine-file-debugger-non-windows, adventuregamestudio/ags#3162
(reworked after Ivan's review on 2026-10-29).

